#. type: Title #
#: docs/sap/events.md:1 docs/sap/events.md:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "SAP Events"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/events.md:8
msgid ""
"Async notifications use envelope `kind: \"evt\"` with a `method` string and "
"`payload`. Either side may send events; most Hub → Satellite events are "
"pushed after an RPC or subscription."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/sap/events.md:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "Stream events (`message.send`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/events.md:12
msgid ""
"After `message.send` returns `stream_id`, Hub pushes `stream.*` events. "
"Defined in [`shared/sap-contract/src/frames/message.ts`](../../shared/sap-"
"contract/src/frames/message.ts) as `streamEventMethods`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (mermaid)
#: docs/sap/events.md:13
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"sequenceDiagram\n"
"  participant Sat as Satellite\n"
"  participant Hub as Hub\n"
"  participant Agent as AgentRuntime\n"
"\n"
"  Sat->>Hub: req message.send\n"
"  Hub->>Sat: res stream_id\n"
"  Hub-->>Sat: evt stream.accepted\n"
"  loop tokens\n"
"    Hub-->>Sat: evt stream.token\n"
"  end\n"
"  Agent->>Hub: tool invocation\n"
"  Hub-->>Sat: evt stream.tool_begin\n"
"  Hub-->>Sat: evt tool.call\n"
"  Sat->>Hub: req tool.result\n"
"  Hub-->>Sat: evt stream.tool_result\n"
"  Hub-->>Sat: evt stream.done\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/events.md:46
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Method                    | Typical payload fields              |\n"
"| ------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n"
"| `stream.accepted`         | `stream_id`                         |\n"
"| `stream.token`            | `stream_id`, `content`              |\n"
"| `stream.content_replace`  | `stream_id`, `content`              |\n"
"| `stream.tool_begin`       | `stream_id`, `tool`, `args`         |\n"
"| `stream.tool_result`      | `stream_id`, `tool`, `content`      |\n"
"| `stream.tool_error`       | `stream_id`, `tool`, `content`      |\n"
"| `stream.awaiting_clarify` | `stream_id`, `items`, `timeout_sec` |\n"
"| `stream.interrupted`      | `stream_id`, `reason`               |\n"
"| `stream.done`             | `stream_id`, optional `reason`      |\n"
"| `stream.error`            | `stream_id`, `error`                |\n"
"| `stream.ping`             | `stream_id`                         |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/events.md:48
msgid ""
"Mapping helpers: `mapRuntimeStreamEventToSap`, `mapSapStreamMethodToApi` in "
"the same file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/sap/events.md:49
#, no-wrap
msgid "SAP stream → Console SSE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/events.md:52
msgid ""
"Satellites that expose HTTP SSE to a browser can reuse the same event names "
"via `mapSapStreamMethodToApi`:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (mermaid)
#: docs/sap/events.md:53
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"flowchart LR\n"
"  subgraph sap [SAP evt]\n"
"    StreamToken[\"stream.token\"]\n"
"    StreamDone[\"stream.done\"]\n"
"  end\n"
"  subgraph ui [Relay / browser client]\n"
"    TokenEvent[\"token\"]\n"
"    DoneEvent[\"done\"]\n"
"  end\n"
"  StreamToken --> TokenEvent\n"
"  StreamDone --> DoneEvent\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/events.md:68
msgid ""
"Type B satellites fan out Hub `stream.*` events over [`/sap/relay/v1`](../../"
"satellites/pair-programming/server/sap/relay.ts); the browser uses "
"`createSapRelayBrowserClient` and `mapSapStreamMethodToApi`."
msgstr ""

